{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>At the shore of seas.</b> His land shall be upon the shore of seas (Yevamot 45a); חוֹף, as its Targum renders סְפָר, מרק\"א בְּלַעַ\"ז, and he shall be found regularly at the shore of ships at the place of the harbor, for ships bring merchandise there, since Zevulun engaged in commerce and supplied food to the tribe of Yissaschar, while they engaged in Torah. This is what Moses said: ״Rejoice, Zevulun, in your going out, and Yissaschar, in your tents״ (Deuteronomy 33) — Zevulun goes out in commerce, and Yissaschar engages in Torah in tents." "<b>And his flank upon Tzidon.</b> The end of his border shall be near Tzidon. <b>His flank.</b> Its end, as in ״וּלְיַרְכְּתֵי הַמִּשְׁכָּן״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "the la'az מרק\"א is Old French marine, 'seashore'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:07.254867277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}